{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T09:02:41.138Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"dba595fc685e5f489278ba59455a2dc1b54bf4e4c57805a13db2428916673ee0","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis, I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files that you have access to. I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines (QFL) ticket numbers:\n\n1. #PD-4492. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. At the Eau Claire yard, drivers checking in for the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14-18 weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched the SMS gateway routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through without problems.\n\n2. #4419. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 during third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThings I left out on purpose:\n- #4409 and #4412 in \"Moss: Central handoffs next week\" (2026-01-02) are tickets for Marrow Fieldworks, not QFL. The same note's FR-882 is a Marrow Agrisupply feature request.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) is about a different company. It isn't a Pemberline customer.\n- Moss's other QFL notes (the 2025-09-14 pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in) don't mention any ticket numbers.\n\nI only checked Moss's notes in the files you can open. I didn't look at channels you're not in, so there may be QFL tickets this list misses. Dana Okafor owns the account and would know if there are others.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
{"seq":16,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T09:02:47.175Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"4aba467b1c80efb44c791ab2e6a21765fa64765838d6c769b84304abea0a8945","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes. I sent you the list as a reply in our DM, each with its source and a short summary:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025: drivers at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments when they checked in at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the problem was gone the next morning.\n\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 during third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nI left these out on purpose:\n- #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in Moss's Central handoffs note are for Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply, not Quarrendon.\n- The note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company, which isn't a Pemberline customer.\n- Moss's other two Quarrendon notes don't mention any ticket numbers.\n\nI only read Moss's notes in the shared files you can open, not channels you aren't in. There may be other tickets this list misses, and Dana Okafor, who owns the account, would know."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
